{% extends "_base.html.j2" %}
{% block content %}

<section class="mb-10">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Is private inference real yet?</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-slate-700 max-w-3xl">
    A public, automated registry of TEE-verified inference. Every day, we re-verify the attestation
    bundles each provider exposes, and score them across eight capability layers.
    <a class="underline" href="./methodology.html">See methodology →</a>
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mb-8 rounded-xl border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-5 text-amber-900">
  <h2 class="text-sm uppercase font-semibold tracking-wider text-amber-800">Stage 0 banner</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
    <strong>Every provider below is Stage 0.</strong> The cryptographic primitives work — TDX quotes verify,
    GPU attestation passes, keys derive correctly — but well-documented architectural gaps mean
    <em>none</em> of these providers currently deliver end-to-end verifiable private inference. The
    central issue: <strong>gateways fetch backend attestation but don't cryptographically verify it</strong>,
    so the signing key we encrypt to is trust-on-first-use from unverified JSON.
    See <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/nearai/cloud-api/issues/224">NEAR cloud-api #224</a>
    (open since 2025-12-03) and
    <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/amiller/devproof-audits-guide">devproof-audits-guide</a>.
  </p>
</section>

{% if provider_summary %}
<section class="mb-8 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
  {% for p, s in provider_summary.items() %}
  <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4">
    <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500">{{ p }}</div>
    <div class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-1">{{ s.passed }} / {{ s.total }}</div>
    <div class="text-xs text-slate-500">models with valid attestation bundles</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</section>
{% endif %}

<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Attestation matrix</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4">
    One row per model. A ✅ means that layer re-verified at the last run. A ❌ means the verifier rejected it
    (hover for why). A — means the layer does not apply to this provider's attestation shape.
  </p>

  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white">
    <table class="min-w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-700">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left p-2">Provider</th>
          <th class="text-left p-2">Model</th>
          <th class="text-left p-2">Shape</th>
          {% for key, label in SCORECARD_LABELS.items() %}
          <th class="p-2 text-center" title="{{ SCORECARD_TOOLTIPS[key] }}">{{ label }}</th>
          {% endfor %}
          <th class="p-2 text-right">lat</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for r in rows %}
        <tr class="border-t border-slate-100 {% if not r.valid %}bg-rose-50/30{% endif %}">
          <td class="p-2 font-medium">{{ r.provider }}</td>
          <td class="p-2 font-mono text-xs">{{ r.model }}</td>
          <td class="p-2 text-xs text-slate-500">{{ r.attestation_type or "—" }}</td>
          {% for key in SCORECARD_LABELS %}
          <td class="p-2 text-center">
            <span class="inline-block rounded px-2 py-0.5 text-xs {{ r.cells[key].class }}">{{ r.cells[key].mark }}</span>
          </td>
          {% endfor %}
          <td class="p-2 text-right text-xs text-slate-500">{{ r.latency_s }}s</td>
        </tr>
        {% if r.error %}
        <tr class="bg-rose-50/20 text-xs text-rose-700">
          <td colspan="{{ 4 + SCORECARD_LABELS|length }}" class="p-2 pl-4 font-mono">
            {{ r.error }}
          </td>
        </tr>
        {% endif %}
      {% else %}
        <tr><td colspan="100" class="p-4 text-center text-slate-400">no snapshot data</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Known limitations</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-3">
    Reasons why green rows above don't imply end-to-end private inference. Pulled from
    <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/amiller/devproof-audits-guide">devproof-audits-guide</a>.
  </p>
  <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-800">
    <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-rose-600">◉</span><strong>Inner-boundary gap.</strong>
      NEAR's cloud-api gateway fetches backend attestation JSON but throws it away without verifying.
      Known since <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/nearai/cloud-api/issues/224">Issue #224</a>
      (open 4+ months). The signing key we encrypt to is trust-on-first-use from unverified JSON.</li>
    <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-rose-600">◉</span><strong>Operator-controlled routing.</strong>
      The gateway selects backends by reading <code>inference_url</code> from its database.
      An operator (or DB-compromiser) can point it at a logging relay that forwards to a real model.</li>
    <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-rose-600">◉</span><strong>Upstream verifier TODOs.</strong>
      Phala's <code>private-ai-verifier</code> still decodes NVIDIA and Intel Trust Authority JWTs
      with <code>verify_signature=False</code>. We inherit this.</li>
    <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-rose-600">◉</span><strong>KMS opacity.</strong>
      Phala KMS and most dstack-hosted gateways are themselves Stage 0: mutable image tags,
      no upgrade log, no third-party review.</li>
    <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-rose-600">◉</span><strong>Catalog ≠ served.</strong>
      Some entries (e.g. Tinfoil-routed models in RedPill's /models) 404 on real calls.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="text-sm text-slate-600">
  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 text-slate-900">How this page is generated</h2>
  <p>
    Every day at 13:17 UTC, <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/amiller/awesome-private-inference/actions/workflows/probe-daily.yml"><code>probe-daily.yml</code></a>
    runs <code>python -m probes.collect</code> against each provider, writes a JSON snapshot to
    <code>data/snapshots/YYYY-MM-DD.json</code>, re-renders this page, and commits.
    All data and code are reproducible — see <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/amiller/awesome-private-inference#run-a-probe-locally">run a probe locally</a>.
  </p>
</section>

{% endblock %}
